# release/scan-rules/private.rules — patterns that must never appear in a release image.
# Format: <id> <tab> <grep -E -i pattern>
# Scanned on: rootfs readback (unsquashfs), raw image bytes (strings), and the
# git-tracked source tree. Exemptions: release/scan-rules/allow.list (path regex + reason).
#
# The maintainer's own list also pins the factory MACs / serials / SSIDs of the lab
# units and the developer network; those entries are not published. Add your own
# unit identifiers below before running release/gate.sh.
#
# ---- unit identity (fill in your own) ----
# mac.unit	<your WAN MAC, e.g. 90[:-]?d3[:-]?cf[:-]?xx[:-]?xx>
# serial.unit	<your factory serial, e.g. 70KWxxxx>
ssid.oem	SpectrumSetup|Setup-[0-9A-F]{4}\b
# ---- credentials ----
cred.binding	binding\.key
cred.ha	webhook_id|homeassistant.*token|Bearer [A-Za-z0-9._-]{20,}
cred.privkey	BEGIN (RSA |EC |OPENSSH )?PRIVATE KEY
# ---- build/vendor leftovers that customers must not see ----
brand.qwrt	QWRT
